rules_version = '2';

// ChartPilot Firestore Security Rules -- spec §73 ("no open/test rules").
//
// DENY BY DEFAULT. These rules block every direct client (mobile/web SDK, REST,
// or any caller authenticating as an end-user) read and write to every path in
// this database. There is no exception carved out for `runs/*` or its
// `claims`/`evidence` subcollections.
//
// Why deny everything:
//   - The backend worker (Cloud Run, Phase 18) reads/writes Firestore via the
//     **Admin SDK** (`google.cloud.firestore.Client`, see
//     `backend/app/storage/firestore_repo.py`), authenticated as a dedicated
//     service account with `roles/datastore.user`. The Admin SDK connects with
//     elevated server credentials and **bypasses these Security Rules entirely** --
//     that is a property of how the Admin SDK authenticates, not something these
//     rules grant or could grant.
//   - The browser/frontend must NEVER read `runs/{run_id}/patients/{patient_id}`,
//     its `claims` subcollection, or its `evidence` subcollection directly from
//     Firestore. All patient run results are served exclusively through the
//     authenticated backend API (Phase 13), which applies its own auth/authz
//     checks before returning anything. A client-side Firestore read of clinical
//     data would bypass that layer entirely -- hence deny-by-default here, with
//     no per-collection carve-out.
//
// Deferred to Phase 18/19: exercising these rules against the Firestore Rules
// Emulator (`firebase emulators:start --only firestore`) to prove empirically
// that an unauthenticated/end-user client is rejected on every path shape used
// by this app. That requires the emulator toolchain, which is out of scope for
// this hermetic Phase 12 change. The Phase-12 deliverable is this rules file
// (deny-by-default, no exceptions) plus the data-model separation documented
// above (Admin-SDK-only backend access, API-mediated client access).
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
